/// - otherwise it is encoded as a JSON object with one name/value pair whose name is the
///   type's name and whose value is the recursively encoded value. For Avro's named types
///   (record, fixed or enum) the user-specified name is used, for other types the type
///   name is used.
///
/// For example, the union schema `["null","string","Foo"]`, where `Foo` is a record name,
